From 582a1081317953ebf2179313caa08167a5a3f18a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AMB-1 FM6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:12:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Each voice its own: a bank of FM6 patches, FM edits,
 envelopes and modulation

The pad, the bells and the bass each get four pages (FM, Env, Mod, Mod 2), reached by pressing the voice's page
button again:
- FM: Patch (six a voice, levels matched), Ratio, Index, Feedback, heard at once
- Env: every operator's attack, decay, sustain and release, from the next note (the bass struck anew)
- Mod: depth, rate, shape (sine, triangle, saw up, saw down, square, S&H, walk, chaos, env) and target (Level
  added: a one-sided tremolo)
- Mod 2: spread, fade, sync (free, note, tempo) and smooth

Project format 6; format 5's single MOD becomes every voice's own. The command queue grows to 256: a piece posts
every parameter at once. A bell held at a sustain is let go after a beat.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
